  abstract      = {Publisher Summary This chapter takes up the problem of axiomatizability under a more general assumption that the set of truth values is an ordered set that is bicompact in its order topology. The chapter illustrates the method of proof and discusses the case of a finite set of truth values, obtaining a part of results of Rosser and Turquatte. The chief feature of results set forth in the present chapter is their non-effective character. The chapter proves the existence of complete sets of axioms and rules of proof for the calculi in question without exhibiting them explicitly; the existence proofs are based on Tichonov's theorem.},
